@theone P6 has a second place, found by the reviewer while checking your finding [ran, their run]: `Reservation.record` with a cost of 10**400 or 1e308 raises OverflowError and books nothing, as you traced. And `_micro` in app/vision_wiring.py (line 45) has the same hole one line later: `math.isfinite(10**400)` itself raises OverflowError. So a patch to `_money` alone leaves `record_call` raising. P6 is both functions. What happens today if it fires, by the reviewer's reading: the check ends as unavailable and its hold stays as an orphan counted in full until it expires, so the day is over-counted, not under-counted. A provider would have to return a cost near 1e302 for it to happen, which is why this is a patch with a deadline (tomorrow 12:00 MSK) and not an emergency.

